# FTE Engine Binary Copy Procedure

After building the FTE engine in the `/fteqw/` directory using `build_m_rel_ccache.sh`, copy the compiled binaries to the **Nuclide root** directory. The nuclide root is the actual runtime location (it sits beside `base/`, `libcef.dll`, `locales/`, etc.), so this is where the binaries must land for the game to use them.

## Build Command

From the fteqw directory, run:
```bash
cd fteqw
bash build_m_rel_ccache.sh
```

This outputs binaries to: `fteqw/engine/release/`

If `cef.c` (the CEF plugin) was changed, also rebuild the plugin:
```bash
cmd /c fteqw\rebuild_cef_plugin.bat
```

## Binary Copy Procedure

After a successful build, copy these files to the nuclide root:

### Main Engine Binary
- **Source**: `fteqw/engine/release/fteqw64.exe`
- **Destination**: `nuclide/fteqw64.exe`

### CEF Plugin (if built)
- **Source**: `fteqw/engine/release/fteplug_cef_x64.dll`
- **Destination**: `nuclide/fteplug_cef_x64.dll`

### Copy Commands (PowerShell, run from nuclide root)

```powershell
$src = "..\fteqw\engine\release"
Copy-Item -LiteralPath "$src\fteqw64.exe"          -Destination "fteqw64.exe"          -Force
Copy-Item -LiteralPath "$src\fteplug_cef_x64.dll"  -Destination "fteplug_cef_x64.dll"  -Force
```

## Directory Structure

```
nuclide/                          (runtime root - active gamedir is base/)
├── fteqw64.exe                   (updated)
├── fteplug_cef_x64.dll           (updated)
├── libcef.dll, locales/, ...     (CEF runtime)
└── base/web/h3-main-menu/        (game:// asset content)

fteqw/ (sibling directory)
└── engine/
    └── release/
        ├── fteqw64.exe           (source)
        └── fteplug_cef_x64.dll   (source)
```

## Notes

- The nuclide root is what the game actually runs; copy here (NOT into `ThirdParty/`).
- The `game://` CEF scheme resolves relative to the active gamedir (`base/`), so the
  binaries must run from the nuclide root for h3-main-menu assets to be found.
- Always copy after successful builds to keep them in sync.
- The CEF plugin copy is only needed if `cef.c` (the plugin) changed.
